  "body": "Wanted: the LinuxCNC post header clears a `G92` offset and states `G97`.\n\nToday the header (`assets/posts/linuxcnc.cps:417`) and the preamble (`:570`) write the modal state with no `G92.1`, and no `G97` comes before the first `S.. M3` (`:590`). A `G92` offset or `G96` left on the control from earlier work applies to the program. No mill post writes these words today. The Haas startup gaps in #1977 are the same class.\n\nFound by the post audit against the LinuxCNC manuals (#4130).\n\nDone means: the header writes `G92.1` (or an option selects it) and `G97` before the first spindle start, and a test pins it.\n",
